+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 2ea1b126e2 (crbug 571126471), missing from the 3.0.1 parser series
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 24-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0006`). Main 2ea1b126e2
+(#110518, 09-10-2026, Toon Verwaest; bug 571126471), not merged to 15.6 (15.9 has it from its branch point). Applied
+as is to 15.6.75.66. Severity not published.
+
+- **Why now:** the CVE-2026-121082 parser series ported in 3.0.1 (21 commits, see the 3.0.1 section) assumed this
+  commit: upstream it landed seven minutes before 618b7515c6, and its `RecordDeclarationError` guard is what
+  618b7515c6 and 7f9cb9e341 rely on. Without it a later arrow head error overwrote the first one, so the series' own
+  tests `es6/regress-arrow-cover-grammar-scope` and `es6/regress-strict-param-error-order` failed on the message
+  text since 3.0.2 (D8-LINUX, every run).
+- `ArrowHeadParsingScope::RecordDeclarationError` keeps the first error (`expression-scope.h`, added to its
+  existing patch). `BaseConsumedPreparseData::GetDataForSkippableFunction` gets `CHECK_GT(end_position,
+  start_position)` and `Scanner::SeekForward` gets `CHECK_GE(pos, current_pos)`, both release CHECKs: corrupted
+  in-sandbox PreparseData can no longer rewind the scanner (sandbox hardening). Test
+  `sandbox/regress-571126471.js` (needs `--sandbox-testing`).
+- `preparse-data.cc` and `scanner.cc` are not touched by any other `patches/v8` file.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): mjsunit `es6/regress-arrow-cover-grammar-scope`, `es6/regress-strict-param-error-order` (now
+green), `sandbox/regress-571126471` with the sandbox testing flags, `es6/*`, `regress/regress-567222737*` and `parser*`.
+
 # FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 78d94a8570 (crbug 586878505), ported from the M159 merge
 
